  "notes": "Cash basis village; one governmental fund (General Fund, p4, single column) and one proprietary fund (Combined Utilities Fund, p6). Governmental receipts/disbursements from p4; fund balance 630,967 -> 660,360. Beginning cash not printed (null); ending cash = governmental funds statement total assets p3 (cash and investments in bank 654,962 + county treasurer 5,398), as FY2023 does. Printed General Fund receipt lines add to 1,000 less than every printed total (p2, p4, p7): recorded as printed, see report_discrepancies. Capital outlay on p4 has no function printed (Statement of Activities allocates it to functions) -> plain 'Capital Outlay'. Business-type from the cash-basis proprietary statement p6 (no single printed total: operating + nonoperating receipts/disbursements summed); Water Project Grant 24,837 and Loan principal payments - NDEQ 13,566 are printed under Other Financing Sources (Uses) -> business_type.other_financing 11,271 as printed (the p2 Statement of Activities counts the grant as intergovernmental and the loan payment in disbursements 295,556). Business-type roll: 563,607 + 335,028 - 281,990 + 11,271 = 627,916. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement p3 (ties to government-wide 660,360), business-type lines from p1 Business-type column; totals from p1 Total column. Detail: all-funds budget schedule p7, per fund column (General Fund, Combined Utilities Fund); the budget column is printed for all funds combined, so budget_final is given only on rows where a single fund has the amount (null otherwise). Utilities budget section 'Other financing sources' (capital user charges, Water Project Grant) recorded as section other financing as printed. Read pages 1-7 of 7"
}
